      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, it definitely adds that layer of tragedy. To make the dialogue and the \"world-building\" even more authentic, I want to dive into the specific social mechanics. \n\nHow would his leadership style be influenced by those cultural values you mentioned? For example, would there be certain traditional or religious undertones to how he treats his subordinates or how he views his \"duty\" to the community versus the law? I want to avoid the trope of him just being a lone wolf; I'm looking for those specific cultural ties that make the organization feel like an extension of his identity.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
